      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.489,
            0.419,
            0.573,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": "(Why ?)"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.104,
            0.127,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "82"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.139,
            0.595,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": "**Theorem 6.2 :** If a line divides any two sides of a triangle in the same ratio, then the line is parallel to the third side."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.203,
            0.594,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": "This theorem can be proved by taking a line DE such that $\\frac { \\mathrm { A D } } { \\mathrm { D B } }   =   \\frac { \\mathrm { A E } } { \\mathrm { E C } }$ and assuming that DE is not parallel to BC (see Fig. 6.12)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.298,
            0.594,
            0.338
          ],
          "content": "If DE is not parallel to BC, draw a line DE parallel to BC."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.608,
            0.138,
            0.898,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.703,
                0.313,
                0.802,
                0.333
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 6.12"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.363,
            0.135,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.323,
            0.346,
            0.572,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": "\\left[ \\frac{ AD }{ DB } = \\frac{ AE '}{ E ' C } \\right.\\tag{Why ?}",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.42,
            0.205,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.326,
            0.405,
            0.45,
            0.45
          ],
          "content": "\\left[ \\frac{ AE }{ EC } = \\frac{ AE '}{ EC } \\right.",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.457,
            0.898,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm { E ^ { \\prime } }$ must coincide. (Why ?)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.502,
            0.772,
            0.522
          ],
          "content": "Let us take some examples to illustrate the use of the above theorems."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.534,
            0.898,
            0.601
          ],
          "content": "**Example 1 :** If a line intersects sides AB and AC of a $\\Delta   \\mathrm { A B C }$ at D and E respectively and is parallel to BC, prove that $\\frac{ AD }{ AB } = \\frac{ AE }{ AC }$ (see Fig. 6.13)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.611,
            0.205,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.336,
            0.611,
            0.896,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": "DE  \\parallel  BC\\tag{Given}",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.657,
            0.134,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.643,
            0.446,
            0.727
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{ AD }{ DB } = \\frac{ AE }{ EC }\\tag{or,}",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.695,
            0.445,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "{ \\frac { \\mathrm { D B } } { \\mathrm { A D } } } = { \\frac { \\mathrm { E C } } { \\mathrm { A E } } }\\tag{or,}",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_19.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.745,
            0.479,
            0.829
          ],
          "content": "\\left\\{ { \\frac { \\mathrm { D B } } { \\mathrm { A D } } } + 1 = { \\frac { \\mathrm { E C } } { \\mathrm { A E } } } + 1 \\right.\\tag{or,}",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.325,
            0.797,
            0.445,
            0.84
          ],
          "content": "{ \\frac { \\mathrm { A B } } { \\mathrm { A D } } } =   { \\frac { \\mathrm { A C } } { \\mathrm { A E } } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.868,
            0.133,
            0.887
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.325,
            0.854,
            0.445,
            0.897
          ],
          "content": "\\left[ { \\frac { \\mathrm { A D } } { \\mathrm { A B } } } = { \\frac { \\mathrm { A E } } { \\mathrm { A C } } } \\right]",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_23.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.755,
            0.656,
            0.898,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": "(Theorem 6.1)"
        },
        {
